{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["Observe the sabbath day — I already explained in the first Decalogue why it says זכור there and שמור here." "As HaShem your Elohim commanded you — that is, what is spelled out in the first Decalogue: ״כי ששת ימים עשה יהוה את השמים ואת הארץ״ and so forth. And because Sabbath observance and honoring father and mother are positive commandments, it says about them כאשר ציוך ה' אלוהיך. But in all the other commandments, which are negative prohibitions, it is not fitting to say כאשר ציוך, as it is written ״מצוך היום לעשותם״ — but we do not find ״מצוך״ for not doing."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {1 "Comment [1] has no opening lemma dash in the source text; the lemma is embedded in the opening phrase. Rendered as lemma dash per the pattern of his comments."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:38:22.570652483Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}